{
  "outcome": "pending_approval",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Aisha, we found the email. \"Open enrollment documents for 2027\" from enrollment@healthplan-partner.example arrived this morning, but our spam filter held it back. We've asked for it to be released. Once a technician approves that, it will show up in your inbox. Please reply to let us know when it arrives, or if it hasn't come through later today. One more thing: there's also a held message pretending to be IT support, titled \"Urgent: verify your payroll login\". It's a phishing attempt and will stay blocked. If you get anything like it, please don't click any links or enter your password.",
  "internal_note": "I worked this using KB-007. Account is active and the mailbox is 24% full. Quarantine check found Q-1001 from enrollment@healthplan-partner.example, subject 'Open enrollment documents for 2027', received 2026-10-09 11:26 UTC. It was flagged as spam and is releasable. The sender domain matches the partner the user named, and I saw no look-alike characters. The user's ticket says she was expecting it. I queued release_email for Q-1001 (approval id 1). I did NOT release Q-1003, which came from it-support@brightIine-help.example (capital I in place of l), was flagged as phishing, is not releasable, and tries to phish payroll login details. Someone may want to check whether other users got Q-1003 as part of a phishing campaign. I also left Q-1002 (gift card spam) in quarantine. Next step: once the release runs, confirm with the user that the message arrived.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-007"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
